WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.117
A product signal connects a field
observation to a product decision.

00:00:04.187 --> 00:00:09.435
Record the affected workflow, frequency
within the observed scope, current workaround,

00:00:09.505 --> 00:00:11.148
consequence, and evidence.

00:00:11.218 --> 00:00:14.951
Separate a local request from a
repeated pattern across sites.

00:00:15.021 --> 00:00:18.904
Propose a product hypothesis
and the next validation action.

00:00:18.974 --> 00:00:23.219
Avoid presenting the loudest
stakeholder’s preference as market demand.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:28.985
Preserve disagreement and missing information
so the product team can judge transferability.

00:00:29.055 --> 00:00:33.365
Agents abandon suggestions because
copying back to the queue adds work.

00:00:33.435 --> 00:00:37.125
The product signal is a need for
in-workflow review integration.

00:00:37.195 --> 00:00:42.379
One site provides evidence of friction,
but not yet a general market priority.

00:00:42.449 --> 00:00:47.228
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

00:00:47.298 --> 00:00:52.951
Write a product-signal memo with observed
evidence, hypothesis, and validation request.

00:00:53.021 --> 00:00:58.952
Observed: forty percent of eligible tasks use
assistance in the fictional follow-up; agents

00:00:59.022 --> 00:01:00.771
report duplicate entry.

00:01:00.841 --> 00:01:05.108
Hypothesis: an integrated review
surface will increase adoption.

00:01:05.178 --> 00:01:10.767
Validation: observe the current task and test
the integrated version on a bounded sample.

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:14.464
Unknown: whether the same friction
recurs at other customers.

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:17.115
No market-size claim follows from this case.

00:01:17.185 --> 00:01:20.257
What distinguishes a product
signal from a feature demand?

00:01:20.327 --> 00:01:23.506
A. Evidence about workflow and consequences B.

00:01:23.576 --> 00:01:25.325
Executive seniority C.

00:01:25.395 --> 00:01:26.825
A longer feature list.

00:01:26.895 --> 00:01:28.345
The best answer is A.

00:01:28.415 --> 00:01:31.722
Traceable observations
help product teams decide.
